hi there steve kaufman here again  today i want to talk about  staying in the moment when we learn  languages  um  you know  there's you can google and look up  living in the moment staying in the  moment  and i think today it's so easy to be  distracted uh it's easy to be distracted  when you're on a computer and have  access to the internet to your email or  to  other places you want to go  it's easy to be distracted by  thinking of  maybe mistakes you made or  things you want to do tomorrow or  frustrations with your language learning  so  i find that it's very important to to  develop that ability to be in the moment  when we are enjoying our language so for  me that might mean  uh when i'm  linking a korean text or i'm reading a  ukrainian text  um that i want to basically block  everything out and just enjoy it  i find now too that i'm sort of  semi-retired  um of course i have a lot of memories of  things but i try not to spend my time on  the past or the future i like to sort of  say wow look at the colors even in this  room  uh the texture of what i'm looking at  um  the sound of the rain outside  just to seize that moment  and to have that kind of an attitude  when you're  enjoying your language listening to it  or  even writing or if you're communicating  with someone just have that sense of  that enjoyment of that moment  don't think about  like i don't recommend that you should  think about wow i'm doing this because  later on it'll improve me that's why i'm  i'm not such a big fan of you know anki  or these other skills where i'm doing  something which is drudgery now but  somehow i think it's going to improve me  i don't tend to think that way i say i'm  doing this now i enjoy it i'm learning  about korea i'm enjoying the sounds of  korean  i'm enjoying that  i happen to know  that this is going to help me  gradually absorb the language i haven't  know that i'm going to just by the mere  fact that i'm exposing myself to more of  the language and reading  and  paying attention to words i know that's  going to help me but i'm not thinking  about what it's going to do for me in  the future i'm only thinking of enjoying  this task while i'm doing it  i find that i've become actually better  in doing that because of my experience  as a language learner so even if i'm  reading spanish now  where i have had trouble with verb  endings as we all do in spanish and  because i'm in the moment i tend to  notice okay this is the third person  singular of the past tense which i  sometimes have trouble with and i kind  of notice it just like  that little tick i noticed i'm in the  moment  that's going to help me i don't think  about how it's going to help me i just  know it's going to help me and so i just  stay in that moment of enjoying the  language so  just a bit of advice i could go on much  longer but i'm trying to keep my videos  short try to enjoy the moment for what  it is rather than for what it might do  for you or thinking about previous  failures or anything else  just enjoy the moment thank you bye for  now
 

